WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.840
AI is being used to help decide whether or not you get that job interview,

00:04.840 --> 00:07.280
how much you pay for your car insurance,

00:07.280 --> 00:09.160
how good your credit score is,

00:09.160 --> 00:12.520
and even what rating you get in your annual performance review.

00:13.280 --> 00:17.360
But these decisions are all being filtered through its assumptions

00:17.360 --> 00:22.440
about our identity, our race, our gender, our age.

00:24.520 --> 00:26.800
How is that happening?

00:26.880 --> 00:30.360
Now, imagine an AI is helping a hiring manager

00:30.360 --> 00:33.280
find the next tech leader in the company.

00:33.280 --> 00:36.440
So far, the manager has been hiring mostly men,

00:36.440 --> 00:41.840
so the AI learns men are more likely to be programmers than women.

00:41.840 --> 00:47.680
And it's very shortly from there to men make better programmers than women.

00:47.680 --> 00:51.480
We have reinforced our own bias into the AI,

00:51.480 --> 00:55.280
and now it's screening out female candidates.

00:57.280 --> 01:01.520
Hang on, if a human hiring manager did that, we'd be outraged.

01:01.520 --> 01:02.680
We wouldn't allow it.

01:02.680 --> 01:06.160
This kind of gender discrimination is not OK.

01:06.160 --> 01:10.680
And yet, somehow, AI has become above the law

01:10.680 --> 01:13.160
because the machine made the decision.

01:14.160 --> 01:15.720
That's not it.

01:15.720 --> 01:21.240
We are also reinforcing our bias in how we interact with AI.

01:21.240 --> 01:26.760
How often do you use a voice assistant like Siri, Alexa or even Cortana?

01:27.240 --> 01:29.840
They all have two things in common.

01:29.840 --> 01:33.000
One, they can never get my name right.

01:33.000 --> 01:36.800
And second, they are all female.

01:36.800 --> 01:39.600
They're designed to be your obedient servants,

01:39.600 --> 01:43.520
turning your lights on and off, ordering your shopping.

01:43.520 --> 01:46.840
You get male AIs too, but they tend to be more high-powered,

01:46.840 --> 01:49.960
like IBM Watson making business decisions,

01:49.960 --> 01:54.600
Salesforce Science Team or Ross, the robot lawyer.

01:54.600 --> 01:58.480
So, poor robots, even they suffer from sexism in the workplace.

02:00.880 --> 02:03.760
Think about how these two things combine

02:03.760 --> 02:09.120
and affect a kid growing up in today's world around AI.

02:09.120 --> 02:12.040
So, they're doing some research for a school project,

02:12.040 --> 02:15.120
and they Google images of CEO.

02:15.120 --> 02:18.040
The algorithm shows them results of mostly men.

02:18.040 --> 02:20.640
And now, they Google personal assistant.

02:20.640 --> 02:24.040
As you can guess, it shows them mostly females.

02:24.040 --> 02:27.680
And then, they want to put on some music and maybe order some food.

02:27.680 --> 02:31.480
And now, they're barking orders at a female voice,

02:31.480 --> 02:34.120
an obedient female voice assistant.

02:35.920 --> 02:41.200
Some of our brightest minds are creating this technology today,

02:41.200 --> 02:45.400
technology that they could have created in any way they wanted.

02:45.400 --> 02:51.120
And yet, they've chosen to create it in the style of 1950s Mad Men Secretary.

02:51.120 --> 02:52.120
Yay!

02:53.120 --> 02:54.560
But okay, don't worry.

02:54.560 --> 02:56.480
This is not going to end with me telling you

02:56.480 --> 03:01.080
that we're all heading towards sexist racist machines running the world.

03:01.080 --> 03:07.640
The good news about AI is that it is entirely within our control.

03:07.640 --> 03:12.480
We get to teach the right values, the right ethics to AI.

03:12.480 --> 03:14.680
So, there are three things we can do.

03:14.680 --> 03:18.040
One, we can be aware of our own biases

03:18.040 --> 03:20.800
and the bias in machines around us.

03:20.800 --> 03:25.360
Two, we can make sure there are diverse teams building this technology.

03:25.360 --> 03:31.160
And three, we have to give it diverse experiences to learn from.

03:31.160 --> 03:34.520
I can talk about the first two from personal experience.

03:34.520 --> 03:39.400
When you work in technology and you don't look like a Mark Zuckerberg or Elon Musk,

03:39.400 --> 03:44.200
your life is a little bit difficult, your ability gets questioned.

03:44.200 --> 03:45.600
Here's just one example.

03:45.600 --> 03:49.400
Like most developers, I often join online tech forums

03:49.400 --> 03:52.640
and share my knowledge to help others.

03:52.640 --> 03:57.960
And I found when I log on as myself with my own photo, my own name,

03:57.960 --> 04:02.560
I tend to get questions or comments like this.

04:02.560 --> 04:06.760
What makes you think you're qualified to talk about AI?

04:06.760 --> 04:10.320
What makes you think you know about machine learning?

04:10.320 --> 04:13.760
So, as you do, I made a new profile.

04:13.760 --> 04:15.680
And this time, instead of my own picture,

04:15.680 --> 04:18.640
I chose a cat with a jetpack on it.

04:18.640 --> 04:22.280
And I chose a name that did not reveal my gender.

04:22.280 --> 04:25.040
You can probably guess where this is going, right?

04:25.040 --> 04:31.440
So, this time, I didn't get any of those patronizing comments about my ability,

04:31.440 --> 04:35.840
and I was able to actually get some work done.

04:35.840 --> 04:37.720
And it sucks, guys.

04:37.720 --> 04:40.240
I've been building robots since I was 15,

04:40.240 --> 04:42.520
I have a few degrees in computer science,

04:42.520 --> 04:48.240
and yet, I had to hide my gender in order for my work to be taken seriously.

04:48.240 --> 04:50.120
So, what's going on here?

04:50.120 --> 04:54.240
Are men just better at technology than women?

04:54.240 --> 04:58.400
Another study found that when women coders on one platform

04:58.400 --> 05:00.800
hid their gender, like myself,

05:00.800 --> 05:04.880
their code was accepted 4% more than men.

05:04.880 --> 05:08.320
So, this is not about the talent.

05:08.320 --> 05:11.240
This is about an elitism in AI

05:11.240 --> 05:15.000
that says a programmer needs to look like a certain person.

